# 17. Glossary

## Purpose

This glossary defines the key governance terms used within the Objective Governance document.

Its purpose is to promote consistent interpretation, communication, and application of governance concepts throughout the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) repository.

---

| Term | Definition |
|------|------------|
| Approval | Formal authorization for an objective or document to become part of the official engineering repository. |
| Authority | The documented source that grants governance responsibility to a document or engineering artifact. |
| Change Management | The controlled process for proposing, reviewing, approving, and implementing changes. |
| Classification | The organization of System Objectives into approved engineering categories. |
| Compliance | Conformance with the governance requirements established by approved engineering documents. |
| Governance | The framework of rules, responsibilities, and processes used to manage engineering artifacts. |
| Lifecycle | The defined sequence of stages through which an engineering artifact progresses from creation to retirement. |
| Objective | A statement describing what the system must achieve without prescribing how it will be implemented. |
| Objective Category | A grouping of objectives according to their primary engineering purpose. |
| Objective Identifier | The permanent, unique identifier assigned to a System Objective. |
| Repository | The structured collection of engineering documents, records, and knowledge that make up the AVIA project. |
| Scope | The boundaries defining what a document governs and what it does not govern. |
| Solution Independence | The principle that objectives describe required outcomes rather than implementation methods. |
| Traceability | The ability to follow relationships between engineering artifacts throughout their lifecycle. |
| Version | A uniquely identified revision of an engineering artifact that preserves its development history. |

---

## Glossary Maintenance

New terms may be added through the approved governance and change management process.

Existing definitions shall only be modified following formal engineering review and approval to preserve consistency across the AVIA repository.
